// iosApp/Configurations/Local.xcconfig
//
// Build settings for the iOS local-flavor variant. Sibling of the
// Android `local` product flavor declared in `app/build.gradle.kts`.
//
// This file is the FOUNDATION (Phase 3.1) of a multi-PR build-out
// per the 2026-05-21 operator directive. Registered as a project
// file reference by Phase 3.2 (PR #717) under the iosApp
// Configurations PBXGroup, and consumed as baseConfigurationReference
// by the project-level Debug-Local + Release-Local
// XCBuildConfigurations.
//
// Variable contracts:
//   BUNDLE_ID_SUFFIX        — `.local` so the app installs alongside
//                             the dev variant on a single device.
//                             Applied to PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER in
//                             Phase 3.2.
//   LOCAL_HOST              — Network address the iPhone uses to
//                             reach the operator's local stack.
//                             Default `localhost` works on iOS
//                             Simulator (shares the Mac's network).
//                             For a physical iPhone, operator MUST
//                             override to the Mac's local-network IP
//                             or mDNS hostname at build time:
//                               xcodebuild -configuration Debug-Local \
//                                 LOCAL_HOST=Macbook.local …
//                             KNOWN GOTCHA — see Phase 3.3 scope note:
//                             LiveKitBridge.swift's `isAllowedURL`
//                             allow-list only accepts `localhost` /
//                             `127.0.0.1` for `ws://`. Overriding to
//                             an mDNS hostname is rejected at runtime
//                             until 3.3 extends the allow-list.
// LOCAL_HOST IS THE ONLY KNOB. Nothing else here is read at runtime.
//
// This file used to also declare LOCAL_API_BASE_URL, LOCAL_LIVEKIT_URL,
// LOCAL_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID and LOCAL_FIREBASE_RTDB_URL, documented above
// as though they were live settings. They were not: only LOCAL_HOST is
// forwarded into Info.plist (as `ShyTalkLocalHost`), and every URL is
// computed in Swift from that one value —
//
//   AppEnvironment.swift:67  localApiBaseUrl = "http://\(localHost):3000"
//   AppEnvironment.swift:74  localLiveKitUrl = "ws://\(localHost):7880"
//   AppEnvironment.swift:77  localRtdbUrl    = "http://\(localHost):9000?ns=demo-shytalk"
//
// Editing the deleted keys changed nothing, which is worse than having no
// knob at all because the recipe looks followed — the exact failure mode
// SHY-0275 was filed to remove, left standing for these four siblings.
// Worse, the RTDB key documented a namespace the app does not use:
// `?ns=demo-shytalk-default-rtdb` here versus the shipping
// `?ns=demo-shytalk` in Swift. A maintainer trusting this file would have
// pointed the emulator at the wrong namespace.
//
// To change a port, edit AppEnvironment.swift. To change the host, set
// LOCAL_HOST below. Absence of the four keys is pinned by the test named
// at the bottom of this comment, so they cannot creep back.
//
// WORTH KEEPING — iOS-vs-Android RTDB divergence: the Android Firebase SDK
// auto-derives the namespace from FirebaseOptions, so `app/build.gradle.kts`'s
// local `RTDB_URL` is `http://host:9000` with no `?ns=` query. The iOS SDK
// does NOT auto-derive; without an explicit `?ns=` selector it connects to
// the wrong default namespace. That is why localRtdbUrl carries `?ns=` and
// Android's does not. The divergence is in the SDKs, not the data.
//
// xcconfig syntax notes for future maintainers:
//   - Variable expansion uses `$(VAR)` — NOT `${VAR}` (that's shell).
//   - `//` is the comment introducer.
//   - In Phase 3.2 when this is referenced as a baseConfigurationReference,
//     CocoaPods integration may require an `#include` of the
//     Pods-iosApp.<config>.xcconfig at the top of THIS file. The
//     include MUST go above the variable declarations so the Pods
//     values cascade as the base layer and our values override them.
//
// Pinned by: express-api/tests/scripts/ios-local-xcconfig.test.js

BUNDLE_ID_SUFFIX = .local
LOCAL_HOST = localhost
